{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01Wzg35buhzzba2G7rystiGk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI attempted to run the analysis as instructed, but the pipeline failed due to an unresolved bug from Attempt 2:\n\n**Issue:** The NER (Named Entity Recognition) system is extracting \"--yes\" as a character name from the text \"He! he! he! --he! he! he! --yes, the Amontillado...\". This invalid name is being sent to LLM validation, which returns malformed JSON, causing the entire analysis to fail.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `_is_valid_name()` function in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/proposers/ner.py` (lines 237-257) doesn't check if names start or end with alphabetic characters. The string \"--yes\" passes validation because it has 3 alphabetic characters out of 5 total (60%), which exceeds the 50% threshold.\n\n**Required Fix:** Add a check to reject names that start or end with non-alphabetic characters, as documented in the EVALUATION_STATE.md file.\n\n**State Updated:**\n- Changed phase from `awaiting_analysis` to `awaiting_fix`\n- Documented Attempt 2 analysis run failure\n- Committed changes to git\n\nThe autonomous loop should now proceed to the FIX phase to implement the documented fix before attempting another analysis run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":172,"cache_read_input_tokens":38585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":172,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c288ef5b-e8b2-4cc6-af0a-cbd795e22408","uuid":"3bdeeb31-69db-4dca-a2b5-7dd5ff6dd999"}
